<title>USA: U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. Boxed Beef cut-out at 1500 CDT - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DES MOINES 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boxed beef higher on moderate demand and light to moderate offerings. Select and Choice rib and loin cuts firm, while chuck and round cuts higher. Beef trimmings higher on fairly good demand and light to moderate offerings. - USDA</p>
<p>----</p>
<p>278 Fab Lds  CH 1-3	CH 1-3	SE 1-3	SE 1-3</p>
<p> 76 50s Lds  550/700     700/850     550/700     700/850</p>
<p>27 Grd Lds ---------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Values =     100.86	100.91	 96.99	 96.27</p>
<p>Changes	  0.62	  0.89	  1.09	  1.09</p>
<p>Rib	  159.78	157.91	154.15	153.14</p>
<p>Chuck	 68.66	 68.48	 72.42	 69.69</p>
<p>Round	 87.02	 87.02	 85.53	 85.53</p>
<p>Loin	 158.40	159.89	139.38	140.34</p>
<p>Brisket     60.50	 60.50	 60.79	 60.79</p>
<p>Shrt Plate  66.43	 66.34	 66.65	 66.48</p>
<p>Flank	 57.99	 57.99	 57.23	 57.23</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
